            according to the project workflow.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="dtable__row">
          <div class="dtable__cell dtable__cell--key">Bryan Center Studios</div>
          <div class="dtable__cell">
            You would like access to Duke studio space and equipment through a <a
              class="ext ext--gold"
              href="#">self-service process ↗</a
            >.
          </div>
          <div class="dtable__cell">Reserve studio time and operate the available equipment yourself.</div>
        </div>
        <div class="dtable__row">
          <div class="dtable__cell dtable__cell--key">Work with a CTL Media Producer</div>
          <div class="dtable__cell">
            The project involves studio or on-location production, specialized formats, or more
            involved production planning.
          </div>
          <div class="dtable__cell">
            A Media Producer will plan the shoot with you, support the technical production, and
            complete the edit. Advance scheduling is helpful.
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="note-gold note-gold--gap" data-keep>
        <p class="note-gold__head">Plan ahead for on-location recording</p>
        <p class="note-gold__text note-gold__text--only">
          On-location recording can be a good choice when the setting adds important context. These
          recordings benefit from advance planning with your Media Producer so that location,
          permissions, travel, sound, lighting, and other production details can be considered.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h3 class="h3">A common production starting point</h3>
      <p class="step__p">
        For many teaching videos, a studio recording with a green screen and teleprompter can provide
        a polished starting point while allowing visuals to be composed around the instructor.
      </p>
      <p class="step__p step__p--gap">
        Other approaches may be useful when they support the learning, including interviews,
        discussion panels, Lightboard, demonstrations, animation, or on-location recording. Your
        Learning Experience Designer and Media Producer can help you consider which approach fits
        your video and project scope. <a class="ext ext--gold" href="#"
          >This video examples gallery ↗</a
        > shows each of these as a finished Duke course video, with notes on what each one took to
        produce.
      </p>

      <div class="ask" data-keep>
        <p class="ask__title">Not sure which path applies?</p>
        <p class="ask__body">
          Before scheduling a studio or on-location recording, check with your CTL Project Manager or
          Learning Experience Designer. They can help you understand which recording pathway and next
          steps fit your project.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

